			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Modularize workbench architecture and fix VSCode worker paths\n\nThis commit restructures the Sky UI component layer to improve code organization and fix critical issues with VSCode web worker extension host integration.\n\n**Workbench Modularization:**\n- Splits `BrowserProxy.astro` and `Electron.astro` into dedicated subdirectories with separate files for Bootstrap, Layout, WindPreload, Workbench, and Polyfills (Electron only)\n- Removes deprecated `Wind.astro` workbench and `Native/` directory components (ActivityBar, Editor, Panel, Sidebar, StatusBar, WindWorkbench)\n- Renames `Application.astro` to `index.astro` as the primary entry point\n\n**VSCode Worker Integration Fixes:**\n- Corrects asset paths from `CodeEditorLand/Editor` to `Microsoft/VSCode` to match actual Output structure\n- Adds `ServeWorkerIframe` Vite plugin to serve `webWorkerExtensionHostIframe.html` during development, preventing Astro's SPA fallback from intercepting\n- Adds `ViteIgnoreWorkerUrls` plugin to inject `@vite-ignore` comments for dynamic worker URL imports\n- Explicitly excludes VSCode worker files from bundling in the `External` configuration\n\n**Configuration Consolidation:**\n- Moves `_VSCODE_FILE_ROOT` global script to `Base.astro` layout, eliminating duplication across pages\n- Fixes workbench configuration values: `serverBasePath: \"/\"`, `connectionToken: \"dummy-token\"`, correct `embedderIdentifier` per workbench type\n- Updates TypeScript configuration with improved settings and excludes Output directory from compilation\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Rewrites README.md with comprehensive Sky documentation covering architecture principles, workbench approaches (A1-A3), component breakdown, and integration flows\n\nThis refactor enables proper loading of VSCode's extension host worker, which requires specific iframe and worker assets to be served at exact paths.",
			"SHA": "5bb9b6130901849cd49b02e13669db1fdd9eb440"
		},
